# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.venv312/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# RULE FOR THIS FILE: ignore only what is too big for git or forbidden to
# leave this machine. Where an ignore rule covers a directory that could ever
# hold a .py, the rule is written as `dir/*` with an explicit `!dir/*.py` so
# git can still descend and see the source. A bare `dir/` stops git descending
# at all, which would swallow code silently.
#
# THE CLINICAL STREAM IS FULLY TRACKED. dataset/raw/ (752 MB of ADNI tables,
# ~115 MB packed), dataset/processed/, models/ and catboost_info/ are all in
# the repo so the whole clinical pipeline -- inputs, intermediates, trained
# CatBoost model, SHAP artefacts, training curves -- reproduces from a clone
# alone, with no ADNI re-download. This repo is PRIVATE and must stay private:
# dataset/raw/ is DUA-restricted subject data.

# CatBoost scratch dir. Everything else under catboost_info/ (the loss curves
# and tfevents) is tracked; only the empty scratch area is not.
catboost_info/tmp/

# --- MRI stream: too big for git, transfer out of band ---

# Preprocessed MRI volumes: ~30 MB now but ~4.6 GB at the full cohort, and
# DUA-restricted subject data. Written as `*` rather than `mri_prep/` so that
# any helper script dropped in here stays visible to git.
#
# THE VOLUMES ARE THE ONLY THING EXCLUDED HERE. vol96/ (550 MB) and mni/
# (4.0 GB) stay out; everything else in this directory is small and is what
# makes the MRI stream reproducible from a clone -- mri_index.csv above all,
# since dataset.py reads it to resolve every split and target, and without it
# the MRI code cannot even enumerate the cohort. The m1 reports, params and
# log are the preprocessing audit trail, and qc/ is its visual evidence.
dataset/mri_prep/*
!dataset/mri_prep/*.py
!dataset/mri_prep/*.csv
!dataset/mri_prep/*.json
!dataset/mri_prep/*.log
!dataset/mri_prep/qc/

# MRI download area.
# Deny by default: this directory holds ~27 GB of zips and, after unpacking,
# one NIfTI per subject in dataset/mri_raw/<PTID>/. Only the small provenance
# artefacts below are worth tracking, so new files are ignored unless
# explicitly allowed.
dataset/mri_raw/*
!dataset/mri_raw/*.py
!dataset/mri_raw/selected_scans.csv
!dataset/mri_raw/selected_image_ids.txt
!dataset/mri_raw/ida_search_results_baselineT1.csv

# NEVER commit: _zips/zip_urls.txt holds pre-authenticated IDA download
# URLs. Those UUID links grant the collection to anyone who has them,
# with no login. Covered by the deny-by-default rule above; named here so
# it does not get whitelisted back in by accident.
dataset/mri_raw/_zips/

# Outbound data bundles (multi-GB, ADNI DUA-restricted - never commit)
dataset/*.tar
dataset/*.tar.*

# --- MRI training checkpoints: fetched artefacts, not sources ---

# Weights pulled back from the Kaggle kernel's output (v7/v8/v9). 20 files,
# 2.42 GB, and INDIVIDUALLY up to 398 MB -- past GitHub's hard 100 MB
# per-file limit, so a push carrying them is rejected outright rather than
# merely bloating history. They are regenerable: every one is still served by
# the kernel's own output, addressed by version.
#
# What survives in the repo instead is everything derived from them that is
# small -- the per-checkpoint val predictions under analysis/threshold_refit/
# and the run artefacts under analysis/kaggle_output/ -- so the analysis
# reproduces from a clone even though the weights do not travel with it.
analysis/kaggle_output/**/*.pt

# Pickled cache of the refit results, rebuilt by refit_thresholds.py from the
# per-checkpoint CSVs beside it. Derived, so not tracked.
analysis/threshold_refit/_results.npy
